@page "/"

<PageTitle>OperationsHub</PageTitle>

<div class="py-5">
    <p class="text-uppercase text-primary fw-semibold mb-2">Operations service management</p>
    <h1 class="display-5 fw-semibold">A clear path from request to resolution.</h1>
    <p class="lead text-body-secondary col-lg-8">
        OperationsHub is a secure internal workspace for submitting,
        assigning, tracking, and auditing operational requests.
    </p>

    <div class="alert alert-light border col-lg-8 mt-4" role="status">
        Administrators can manage departments and request types, while teams submit, assign, track, and audit operational requests.
    </div>

    <div class="row g-3 col-xl-10 mt-3" aria-label="OperationsHub capabilities">
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <section class="border rounded-3 h-100 p-3">
                <h2 class="h5">Role-aware workflow</h2>
                <p class="text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    Requesters, technicians, managers, and administrators each receive a focused, server-enforced experience.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <section class="border rounded-3 h-100 p-3">
                <h2 class="h5">Auditable MySQL data</h2>
                <p class="text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    Assignments, state changes, comments, and audit history remain available throughout the request lifecycle.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <section class="border rounded-3 h-100 p-3">
                <h2 class="h5">Continuously verified delivery</h2>
                <p class="text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    The web application and local database run as a health-checked Docker Compose stack, verified by every change.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
